    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d675">

                <pb facs="0726" n="468" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg468"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/2412a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Secretary of Commerce</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Redfield</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-07-13">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 13, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: As you are aware, this Department, since
                    February 19, 1915, in compliance with the request of the German Government, has
                    been transmitting to that Government, through the American Embassy at Berlin,
                    information concerning the sailings and arrivals of American vessels, giving as
                    complete details as possible.</p>
                <p>I now have the honor to advise you, for the information of the Bureau of
                    Navigation, that, although the Department will continue to transmit such
                    information regarding American passenger vessels, it is considered inadvisable
                    at this time to send to the German Government any information concerning the
                    departure and arrival of ships carrying freight only, other than to neutral
                    ports.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
